---
import Base from '../components/layout/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site.js';

const endpoints = ['devices', 'roms', 'support', 'features'];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What Android ROM Compat is, where the data comes from, how to use the API, and the licences."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'About', url: '/about/' }]}
>
  <section>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      A list of which Android ROMs officially support which phones, and what works on each. It only covers official
      builds, and would rather leave a gap than guess, so anything nobody has checked shows as unknown.
    </p>
    <p>
      Device lists were seeded from each ROM's own published list, and every entry links back to its source. Things
      change fast, so anything not checked for a year is marked stale.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="disclaimer">
    <h2 id="disclaimer">Before you flash anything</h2>
    <p>
      Unlocking a bootloader and installing a ROM can wipe your data, brick your phone or void its warranty. This site
      isn't an install guide. Follow the ROM's own instructions for your exact model, and check them first.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="api">
    <h2 id="api">API</h2>
    <p>The whole dataset is available as static JSON, rebuilt on every change. No key, no rate limit.</p>
    <ul>
      {endpoints.map((name) => <li><a href={`/api/${name}.json`}><code>/api/{name}.json</code></a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="licences">
    <h2 id="licences">Licences</h2>
    <p>
      The code is <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT</a>. The data is
      <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/data/LICENSE`}>CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, so you can reuse it as long as you credit this
      project and share alike. ROM names and logos belong to their projects.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
